1
00:00:01,060 --> 00:00:03,240
You could even win a reward!

2
00:00:04,820 --> 00:00:06,620
We don't have any other leads,

3
00:00:06,840 --> 00:00:09,737
so we should at least try
using the Stratumlord coins.

4
00:00:09,820 --> 00:00:11,220
It's a perfect fit.

5
00:00:11,460 --> 00:00:12,340
One problem.

6
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:18,897
The Menagerie of Fools has four coins.

7
00:00:18,980 --> 00:00:21,740
Origin, Dead, Clearflow, Labyrinth.

8
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:23,377
And we're packing three.

9
00:00:23,460 --> 00:00:26,557
Clearflow, Scorching, and lastly, Dark.

10
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:31,405
We have seven coins total, but two are
clear flow and we're missing Dog Mountain.

11
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:33,620
Well, still worth a try.

12
00:00:35,480 --> 00:00:39,304
Looks like it won't let us through
without the Dog Mountain coin.

13
00:00:42,760 --> 00:00:43,780
Hold on a minute.

14
00:00:46,100 --> 00:00:47,240
An old box?

15
00:00:47,760 --> 00:00:49,817
Director Bear said we
should only open this

16
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:52,724
when we had finally made
it to the inner depths.

17
00:00:53,660 --> 00:00:54,490
Jackpot.

18
00:00:54,573 --> 00:00:55,997
Is that the doggy coin?

19
00:00:56,080 --> 00:00:58,700
That Sly Bear came
through for us. Sure did.

20
00:00:59,120 --> 00:01:02,697
I've been told his old team were the
only ones to ever defeat Dog Mountain,

21
00:01:02,780 --> 00:01:04,309
so my hopes were sky high.

22
00:01:04,540 --> 00:01:06,397
He's the biggest and best bear I know!

23
00:01:06,480 --> 00:01:07,357
He's that sexy!

24
00:01:07,440 --> 00:01:09,322
Thanks for the plug device, pal.

25
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:11,080
You're a real MVP, dude.

26
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:31,657
On the outside, I'm just a big metal box,
but inside I've still got a human soul!

27
00:01:31,740 --> 00:01:33,197
In this new world of wonders,

28
00:01:33,280 --> 00:01:36,737
I travel to and fro on the back
of my super strong partner Lamas!

29
00:01:36,820 --> 00:01:38,840
The name's Boxxo! Hello there!

30
00:01:39,100 --> 00:01:40,700
That means yes, by the way!

31
00:01:56,080 --> 00:01:59,377
Chapter 3 I can't afford it I can't

32
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:04,560
afford it I can't afford it For now,

33
00:02:04,840 --> 00:02:08,940
I can't afford it I can
afford it I can't afford it

34
00:02:49,460 --> 00:02:52,577
Before we go, let's make
sure we're on the same page?

35
00:02:52,660 --> 00:02:54,660
About the wishes we want granted.

36
00:02:57,780 --> 00:03:00,540
Our little family only has a single wish.

37
00:03:01,060 --> 00:03:03,480
To remove decay, Kai's negative blessing.

38
00:03:04,140 --> 00:03:05,140
Nothing more.

39
00:03:05,700 --> 00:03:08,417
But if we can get another,
I want a hot girlfriend.

40
00:03:08,500 --> 00:03:11,157
Don't be so selfish, I'll
take one too, extra hot!

41
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:12,400
What about you?

42
00:03:12,920 --> 00:03:15,077
My dearest wish has already come true.

43
00:03:15,160 --> 00:03:17,317
So I'll happily yield
mine to everyone else!

44
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:20,117
If there's a spare, I'll
take a castle of boots.

45
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:21,757
I Don't need anything either.

46
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:23,977
Just let me eat until I'm about to burst!

47
00:03:24,060 --> 00:03:24,997
It we'll call it even?

48
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:28,857
Pity how to wish the mine has
already come true as well.

49
00:03:28,940 --> 00:03:33,297
Well I do have a wish in truth it
is Something I must win for myself.

50
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:34,817
I don't need a thing.

51
00:03:34,900 --> 00:03:36,497
Well llamas.

52
00:03:36,580 --> 00:03:37,977
Nothing for myself.

53
00:03:38,060 --> 00:03:41,097
There is Something I want
but it's not for me to ask.

54
00:03:41,180 --> 00:03:47,257
Guess I'm up to bat.

55
00:03:47,340 --> 00:03:52,777
I know what I Want I
went to eat you again.

56
00:03:52,860 --> 00:03:54,777
Thank you.

57
00:03:54,860 --> 00:03:59,077
Cap goes first.

58
00:03:59,160 --> 00:04:03,737
I'm putting my Non-existent foot down.

59
00:04:03,820 --> 00:04:04,677
You sure?

60
00:04:04,760 --> 00:04:07,113
But there's a chance we'll only get one.

61
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:14,310
wish.

62
00:04:14,393 --> 00:04:15,223
That's a good point.

63
00:04:15,306 --> 00:04:17,617
There are plenty of other
dungeons in the world.

64
00:04:17,700 --> 00:04:20,157
So if you don't end up getting
your wish granted here,

65
00:04:20,240 --> 00:04:23,177
that just means we get to go
and conquer some other dungeon.

66
00:04:23,260 --> 00:04:26,520
And I'll be with you every
step of the way. Same here.

67
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:28,057
These straps aren't budging.

68
00:04:28,140 --> 00:04:28,970
Where master

69
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:31,357
goes, I follow.

70
00:04:31,440 --> 00:04:33,540
Are we there yet? Pray not.

71
00:04:33,880 --> 00:04:36,017
We've been walking a
while, but it's so dark.

72
00:04:36,100 --> 00:04:38,240
Hard to tell how big this place is.

73
00:04:46,520 --> 00:04:48,226
That's about what I expected.

74
00:04:48,860 --> 00:04:51,272
Now the lights are on, but nobody's home.

75
00:04:51,380 --> 00:04:54,080
You have done well to
make it here, Travers.

76
00:04:55,560 --> 00:04:58,217
As a reward for reaching
the lowest straddle,

77
00:04:58,300 --> 00:05:01,300
I shall grant you whatever
wish your heart desires.

78
00:05:01,460 --> 00:05:03,636
Whoa, he's really gonna do the thing!

79
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:04,990
But first,

80
00:05:05,073 --> 00:05:07,757
I can sense that one of
you standing before me

81
00:05:07,840 --> 00:05:10,605
is more than capable of
threatening my dungeon.

82
00:05:10,960 --> 00:05:12,617
I assume you're referring to me.

83
00:05:12,700 --> 00:05:14,800
I used to work for the Netherlord.

84
00:05:15,620 --> 00:05:16,780
Listen well.

85
00:05:17,060 --> 00:05:21,800
The Netherlord seeks to seize my dungeon
constructed from the sacred tree.

86
00:05:22,240 --> 00:05:24,897
That fool has already
stolen most of my power.

87
00:05:24,980 --> 00:05:26,098
Who's that old guy?

88
00:05:28,360 --> 00:05:30,020
Heed my warning!

89
00:05:31,640 --> 00:05:35,077
Talking purple's a real pain, so
how's about I just give it a rest?

90
00:05:35,160 --> 00:05:37,060
Slap my bum and call me Sally.

91
00:05:37,340 --> 00:05:39,037
Never in a million years did I think some

92
00:05:39,120 --> 00:05:41,557
dumb kiddos would show
up and storm my dungeon.

93
00:05:41,640 --> 00:05:43,522
I was about to go on break, too.

94
00:05:44,140 --> 00:05:48,577
He's giving jaded office worker who hates
his life and copes by trolling in forums.

95
00:05:48,660 --> 00:05:50,677
Not how I pictured the dungeon master.

96
00:05:50,760 --> 00:05:54,277
I take it you're the one in charge
of this nasty little dungeon?

97
00:05:54,360 --> 00:05:56,184
Well, that's one way to put it.

98
00:05:56,340 --> 00:05:58,717
I'm the guy those in the
know call the dungeon master.

99
00:05:58,800 --> 00:06:02,737
Back in the day, they used to throw
around words like genius and visionary,

100
00:06:02,820 --> 00:06:03,650
but I digress.

101
00:06:03,780 --> 00:06:05,309
I'm forgetting my manners.

102
00:06:06,460 --> 00:06:08,100
Oh, look at this table.

103
00:06:08,380 --> 00:06:10,380
Go on, you can rest your keisters.

104
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:13,437
I'm sure you've got a boatload
of questions to ask me.

105
00:06:13,520 --> 00:06:16,237
I'm an open book, so if
it's in my power to answer,

106
00:06:16,320 --> 00:06:18,517
I don't mind giving you
folks the exposition dump.

107
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:20,237
But let's get some snacks going.

108
00:06:20,320 --> 00:06:21,240
Hello there.

109
00:06:25,060 --> 00:06:26,020
Look at that.

110
00:06:26,180 --> 00:06:27,117
It's my lucky day.

111
00:06:27,200 --> 00:06:30,437
I've always been curious about
these here thingamabobbers.

112
00:06:30,520 --> 00:06:34,237
As a stalwart vending machine, I'm
the head honcho of feeding folks.

113
00:06:34,320 --> 00:06:38,908
Plus, taking ownership of edibles keeps
my pals safe from any drink tampering.

114
00:06:39,580 --> 00:06:42,537
Alright, let's hear what
questions you've got cooking.

115
00:06:42,620 --> 00:06:45,857
Okay, so what's the deal with
dungeons and dungeon masters?

116
00:06:45,940 --> 00:06:47,097
Getting right to it.

117
00:06:47,180 --> 00:06:49,877
Dungeons are basically just
vanglorious works of art,

118
00:06:49,960 --> 00:06:53,897
created by ancient wizards to show off
our ancient wizardry, because why not?

119
00:06:53,980 --> 00:06:56,277
Or you could think of them
as recreational facilities.

120
00:06:56,360 --> 00:07:00,420
The Dungeon Master is the
individual who made the dungeon.

121
00:07:00,700 --> 00:07:02,759
Ancient wizards making dungeon art?

122
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:06,017
I don't know, seems like I
would have heard about it.

123
00:07:06,100 --> 00:07:08,780
We wizards died out, for reasons.

124
00:07:09,220 --> 00:07:13,297
As a result, history has forgotten
us and the world with it, I'm afraid.

125
00:07:13,380 --> 00:07:15,037
Old wizards made these dungeons,

126
00:07:15,120 --> 00:07:17,697
to brag about how cool they
were for making dungeons?

127
00:07:17,780 --> 00:07:19,074
Are you being serious?

128
00:07:19,420 --> 00:07:21,017
Never would have guessed
this world had its

129
00:07:21,100 --> 00:07:22,857
own equivalent to modern game developers.

130
00:07:22,940 --> 00:07:25,657
Is it true that for
reaching the lowest level,

131
00:07:25,740 --> 00:07:27,917
you'll grant any wish our hearts desire?

132
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:29,880
Yep, the rumors are true.

133
00:07:31,480 --> 00:07:33,120
How many wishes do we get?

134
00:07:33,460 --> 00:07:36,107
You can technically make
as many as you want.

135
00:07:36,280 --> 00:07:37,398
There's no maximum.

136
00:07:37,660 --> 00:07:41,425
However, that doesn't mean you
can have anything and everything.

137
00:07:41,540 --> 00:07:45,717
Granting a wish consumes an amount of mana
that's proportional to its wow factor,

138
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:48,357
which means your wishes
are only limited by the

139
00:07:48,440 --> 00:07:51,077
amount of mana contained
within this dungeon of mine.

140
00:07:51,160 --> 00:07:55,400
Do you have the power to remove
my son's negative blessing? I do.

141
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:01,750
Do it.

142
00:08:01,833 --> 00:08:04,117
I wish for you to free him from his curse.

143
00:08:04,200 --> 00:08:05,757
Better untwist those britches.

144
00:08:05,840 --> 00:08:08,457
I'm not done explaining
all the fine print yet.

145
00:08:08,540 --> 00:08:12,557
Let's say you wish for a bunch of
silver golden jewels in obscene piles.

146
00:08:12,640 --> 00:08:16,637
I fork over my entire personal treasure
trove without using a single lick of mana.

147
00:08:16,720 --> 00:08:17,940
That said,

148
00:08:18,200 --> 00:08:20,197
removing a negative
blessing is going to eat

149
00:08:20,280 --> 00:08:23,460
up a huge slice of this
dungeon's mana pie. Gotcha.

150
00:08:23,760 --> 00:08:25,525
Then I have one last question.

151
00:08:25,740 --> 00:08:29,600
Can you cure Kai's decay and
also turn Boxo human again?

152
00:08:29,860 --> 00:08:31,980
I can do it by the skin of my teeth.

153
00:08:32,120 --> 00:08:33,137
But after those two,

154
00:08:33,220 --> 00:08:37,573
I'll be completely out of mana and
unable to grant you any further wishes.

155
00:08:37,920 --> 00:08:40,260
Wait, am I about to rejoin humanity?

156
00:08:40,720 --> 00:08:42,037
Is this for you, Boxo?

157
00:08:42,120 --> 00:08:43,917
You deserve every happiness, Master.

158
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:45,157
Congratulations, Boxo.

159
00:08:45,240 --> 00:08:48,005
Now I can make my wish
with a clear conscience.

160
00:08:48,100 --> 00:08:49,060
It's happening!

161
00:08:49,880 --> 00:08:51,586
When's the game for the team?

162
00:08:51,780 --> 00:08:54,537
I had my hopes up, but I never
really thought it would happen.

163
00:08:54,620 --> 00:08:55,700
Pinch me, Lamas!

164
00:08:55,880 --> 00:08:56,720
Be warned.

165
00:08:56,920 --> 00:08:58,897
If I do grant those wishes of yours,

166
00:08:58,980 --> 00:09:02,215
this dungeon will collapse
and crush everything within.

167
00:09:02,900 --> 00:09:03,860
Wouldn't we die?

168
00:09:04,320 --> 00:09:07,417
Damn, we were this close to
making Boxxo human again.

169
00:09:07,500 --> 00:09:11,037
If the dungeon collapses, it'll flatten
my friends into tragic tortillas.

170
00:09:11,120 --> 00:09:14,532
That price is too steep to
make my selfish wish come true.

171
00:09:22,180 --> 00:09:25,157
You want me to start by
removing the boy's negative

172
00:09:25,240 --> 00:09:27,537
blessing Then you'll
evacuate all your little

173
00:09:27,620 --> 00:09:29,677
friends And make the journey back here by

174
00:09:29,760 --> 00:09:32,697
yourself Letting you make
your wish guilt-free He's

175
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:35,297
either amazing at guessing
or he can read my mind

176
00:09:35,380 --> 00:09:37,777
like Kikuyu It seems the
Netherlord has sealed

177
00:09:37,860 --> 00:09:40,597
the dungeon exit just
to be a jerk But I can

178
00:09:40,680 --> 00:09:43,560
temporarily open it again
Then we've got a plan.

179
00:09:43,780 --> 00:09:45,860
Good thinking, Boxo. Hello there.

180
00:09:46,640 --> 00:09:50,480
In that case, I'll go ahead and
remove this boy's curse of decay.

181
00:10:04,220 --> 00:10:05,620
The pain is gone.

182
00:10:06,500 --> 00:10:07,620
It's a miracle.

183
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:10,777
The sports blessing of
decay is gone for good.

184
00:10:10,860 --> 00:10:15,017
He'll never again have to suffer the
torment of feeling his flesh rotting away.

185
00:10:15,100 --> 00:10:16,520
I am in your debt.

186
00:10:16,740 --> 00:10:18,300
At long last, you're free.

187
00:10:18,720 --> 00:10:20,717
There's nothing binding you to me.

188
00:10:20,800 --> 00:10:24,200
I may not need your magic,
but I choose to stay with you.

189
00:10:24,360 --> 00:10:25,654
I hope you don't mind!

190
00:10:31,680 --> 00:10:33,680
I've been waiting for this moment!

191
00:10:34,080 --> 00:10:36,200
So, that's where you were hiding!

192
00:10:44,900 --> 00:10:46,117
Solary, what gift?

193
00:10:46,200 --> 00:10:48,553
I swear I didn't know about any of this.

194
00:10:49,720 --> 00:10:53,660
Even I never expected this
plan to work out so well.

195
00:10:59,920 --> 00:11:02,660
The fruits of victory are sweet.

196
00:11:03,140 --> 00:11:06,375
Granting such a wish drained
a great deal of his power,

197
00:11:06,520 --> 00:11:09,757
I can now finally extinguish
his life with relative ease.

198
00:11:09,840 --> 00:11:11,260
That's a foul trick!

199
00:11:12,280 --> 00:11:17,180
You can't stoop to such depths just
to get past my anti-monster barrier?

200
00:11:17,500 --> 00:11:20,740
I've sent more of your
power away, Dungeon Master.

201
00:11:21,100 --> 00:11:24,860
Your precious dungeon is
practically in the palm of my hand.

202
00:11:25,160 --> 00:11:27,395
You used me to sneak your way in here?

203
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:29,520
You're my property.

204
00:11:29,660 --> 00:11:31,760
Why shouldn't I make use of you?

205
00:11:31,940 --> 00:11:33,577
Don't you dare objectify her!

206
00:11:33,660 --> 00:11:36,240
Saurim, given your loyalty,

207
00:11:36,640 --> 00:11:40,840
I'm willing to make an exception
and allow you to return to my side.

208
00:11:42,300 --> 00:11:46,117
The old me would have been more than
happy to go crawling back to you,

209
00:11:46,200 --> 00:11:48,020
but I'm not that girl anymore.

210
00:11:48,760 --> 00:11:51,584
Now I have something
that's far more dear to me.

211
00:11:53,400 --> 00:11:55,320
Sentimental fool. Audrey!

212
00:11:57,660 --> 00:12:00,397
Oh, you erased it with eye breach.

213
00:12:00,480 --> 00:12:04,598
Can't let you kill off a young lady
who might join our family one day!

214
00:12:04,860 --> 00:12:06,095
What's our next move?

215
00:12:06,280 --> 00:12:08,817
We've got the Captain's
Eye Breach and my barrier.

216
00:12:08,900 --> 00:12:12,488
Paired with their gimmicks, we
might actually stand a chance!

217
00:12:14,260 --> 00:12:19,580
It would be amusing to continue this
battle, but I have already achieved my goal!

218
00:12:19,880 --> 00:12:21,860
Let's begin a different game!

219
00:12:22,240 --> 00:12:24,181
What kind of magic has you there?

220
00:12:24,640 --> 00:12:26,557
Feels like a four on the Richter!

221
00:12:26,640 --> 00:12:28,617
It's freaking them out because
they've never felt an earthquake!

222
00:12:28,700 --> 00:12:32,200
If you keep this up, you'll
cause this dungeon to collapse.

223
00:12:32,520 --> 00:12:34,720
That's exactly what I intend to do.

224
00:12:34,980 --> 00:12:36,660
I got what I came for,

225
00:12:36,840 --> 00:12:40,900
which means I have absolutely no
reason to preserve this place.

226
00:12:41,220 --> 00:12:45,980
I'll move the monsters to the surface
and watch as the humans suffer and die.

227
00:12:48,340 --> 00:12:49,557
What's wrong with you?

228
00:12:49,640 --> 00:12:51,228
Can't you just get a hobby?

229
00:12:51,660 --> 00:12:55,360
Monsters solely exist to
inflict pain and spread sorrow.

230
00:12:55,960 --> 00:12:58,784
Well, the Demon Lord has
strayed from this path.

231
00:12:59,000 --> 00:12:59,880
It's pathetic.

232
00:13:00,340 --> 00:13:04,980
I look forward to seeing which comes
first, the collapse or your demise.

233
00:13:05,540 --> 00:13:06,600
He vanished?

234
00:13:06,940 --> 00:13:08,480
Without killing us off?

235
00:13:11,340 --> 00:13:14,928
Listen, I'm going to conjure a
transfer circle for you folks.

236
00:13:15,060 --> 00:13:18,277
It will transport you back to
the Clearflow Lake Stratum.

237
00:13:18,360 --> 00:13:20,780
Go back there and take everyone with you.

238
00:13:21,040 --> 00:13:22,981
Escape the dungeon while you can.

239
00:13:23,460 --> 00:13:25,166
Man, with my remaining power,

240
00:13:25,280 --> 00:13:28,927
I'll release the door leading
to the surface so you can leave.

241
00:13:31,680 --> 00:13:34,337
I don't know how much
longer my power will last,

242
00:13:34,420 --> 00:13:38,300
so it wouldn't be a bad idea to
hot-foot it out of here, got it?

243
00:13:38,560 --> 00:13:41,913
This old man wizard is going
to sacrifice himself for us?

244
00:13:42,020 --> 00:13:47,740
Hey, Boxo, sorry I couldn't grant
your wish and make you a real boy.

245
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:49,440
You must be devastated.

246
00:13:50,200 --> 00:13:52,560
Ike, ain't for Ike again.

247
00:13:53,800 --> 00:13:55,640
What a fascinating fella.

248
00:13:56,060 --> 00:13:59,942
I'll try to keep the dungeon from
collapsing for as long as I can,

249
00:14:00,060 --> 00:14:02,001
though I can't make any promises.

250
00:14:02,740 --> 00:14:04,720
What about you, dungeon master?

251
00:14:05,400 --> 00:14:07,576
Don't worry, that pretty little head.

252
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:09,040
This is how it works.

253
00:14:09,420 --> 00:14:11,302
Whenever a dungeon is conquered,

254
00:14:11,500 --> 00:14:14,960
the dungeon master grants the
wishes, then vanishes away.

255
00:14:16,620 --> 00:14:18,980
I've lived longer than anyone should.

256
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:25,140
Didn't expect it to end like this, but at
the very least, it's worth a good laugh.

257
00:14:26,320 --> 00:14:32,340
Say, Poxo, I know I wasn't able to
grant that wish of yours, but here,

258
00:14:32,760 --> 00:14:33,780
a parting gift.

259
00:14:37,480 --> 00:14:40,897
May a promising future
await the brave hunters

260
00:14:40,980 --> 00:14:44,000
who I had the honor of
crossing paths with today.

261
00:14:44,740 --> 00:14:50,180
They who conquered the Dungeon of the Sacred
Tree, congratulations on your triumph.

262
00:14:50,500 --> 00:14:54,780
And thank you for enjoying
my dungeon to the very end.

263
00:14:55,300 --> 00:14:58,160
It was a real home and a house.

264
00:15:01,240 --> 00:15:04,157
I never could have imagined
it would come to this.

265
00:15:04,240 --> 00:15:07,117
We need to evacuate everyone
to the Origin Stratum now.

266
00:15:07,200 --> 00:15:08,837
We've got to get them out of this dungeon.

267
00:15:08,920 --> 00:15:09,750
I understand.

268
00:15:11,100 --> 00:15:12,200
Big ball!

269
00:15:13,540 --> 00:15:14,820
We got backup!

270
00:15:15,260 --> 00:15:16,437
Hey, it's the Light Lady!

271
00:15:16,520 --> 00:15:20,337
Lamas, Voxo, our top priority is
securing the door leading outside.

272
00:15:20,420 --> 00:15:21,250
You got it!

273
00:15:21,333 --> 00:15:22,163
Come over here!

274
00:15:22,820 --> 00:15:23,760
Excuse us!

275
00:15:24,020 --> 00:15:25,340
Thank you very much!

276
00:15:39,440 --> 00:15:40,270
Lamas!

277
00:15:40,353 --> 00:15:41,183
Director Bear!

278
00:15:41,266 --> 00:15:42,096
There's trouble!

279
00:15:42,179 --> 00:15:43,009
What's the issue?

280
00:15:43,092 --> 00:15:45,077
Gross monsters are swarming the village!

281
00:15:45,160 --> 00:15:46,219
There's no choice.

282
00:15:46,400 --> 00:15:48,694
We'll have to evacuate in small groups.

283
00:16:06,340 --> 00:16:10,164
I'll turn you all into charcoal
and use you to warm our tootsies!

284
00:16:11,820 --> 00:16:13,800
There's a king frog named!

285
00:16:14,540 --> 00:16:16,500
Freaking out's a waste of energy.

286
00:16:16,880 --> 00:16:21,115
You've got to keep the Tom cool and
collected vibes going to yours, too.

287
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:24,740
Uranu's got game.

288
00:16:37,940 --> 00:16:39,717
We've almost got everyone out.

289
00:16:39,800 --> 00:16:43,212
Me thinks our battle montage
will buy us just enough time.

290
00:16:44,760 --> 00:16:47,172
Dang, I wish I had some wood to knock on.

291
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:50,460
I seem to have underestimated
your team's tenacity.

292
00:16:50,880 --> 00:16:51,920
The big bad.

293
00:16:52,680 --> 00:16:55,040
I find your efforts quite riveting.

294
00:16:55,580 --> 00:16:58,540
So, I'll briefly release
my hold on the door.

295
00:17:07,800 --> 00:17:08,657
It's always something.

296
00:17:08,740 --> 00:17:14,640
The greatest joy in hunting comes from
cornering your prey and watching them squirm.

297
00:17:14,920 --> 00:17:17,096
You're a nasty piece of work, mister.

298
00:17:20,980 --> 00:17:22,800
So, what do we do now?

299
00:17:28,060 --> 00:17:29,160
Please go.

300
00:17:30,080 --> 00:17:31,800
I knew she'd understand.

301
00:17:32,220 --> 00:17:34,180
Now, time for a form change.

302
00:17:34,980 --> 00:17:37,568
Behold the biggest
vending machine in Japan.

303
00:17:39,620 --> 00:17:40,450
Hmm.

304
00:17:40,533 --> 00:17:43,680
You dare to defy me, magic
item known as Boxlow?

305
00:17:43,980 --> 00:17:48,340
Even though we're both well aware, you
cannot maintain that form for long.

306
00:17:48,680 --> 00:17:49,560
That's a fact.

307
00:17:49,860 --> 00:17:52,777
Using my barrier in this form
is blowing through my points.

308
00:17:52,860 --> 00:17:54,420
Good thing I'm loaded now.

309
00:17:54,680 --> 00:17:56,097
I've got points to spare.

310
00:17:56,180 --> 00:17:57,220
Thanks to him!

311
00:17:57,420 --> 00:17:59,900
The least I can do is fill your coffers.

312
00:18:00,240 --> 00:18:02,900
Please add this gift to your point total.

313
00:18:03,100 --> 00:18:06,660
The Dungeon Master gifted me
his entire treasure trove.

314
00:18:07,420 --> 00:18:10,037
You wouldn't believe how
many zeros I'm packing!

315
00:18:10,120 --> 00:18:13,317
I'll keep this barrier up until
every last person gets away!

316
00:18:13,400 --> 00:18:14,280
Hey, Voxo!

317
00:18:14,460 --> 00:18:15,657
What do you think you're doing?

318
00:18:15,740 --> 00:18:17,997
You're gonna get left
behind if you don't stop!

319
00:18:18,080 --> 00:18:20,697
She's not gonna like this,
but it's the only way!

320
00:18:20,780 --> 00:18:25,280
Leave the int to my indigo! I refuse!

321
00:18:25,540 --> 00:18:26,737
I'm not leaving your side!

322
00:18:26,820 --> 00:18:28,437
If you're staying, I am too!

323
00:18:28,520 --> 00:18:32,837
Voxo has a better chance of coming back
safely if we're not around to distract him.

324
00:18:32,920 --> 00:18:34,800
That's it, right? Yes!

325
00:18:35,300 --> 00:18:38,560
I can't leave him! We're
a team. Don't be silly.

326
00:18:38,880 --> 00:18:40,577
You know we'd only be in the way.

327
00:18:40,660 --> 00:18:45,280
So put your faith in him, and
let's go. I don't wanna. I can't.

328
00:18:45,860 --> 00:18:47,400
Don't be sad, Lamas.

329
00:18:47,840 --> 00:18:50,600
Dying's not on my Dead
list, but winning is.

330
00:18:50,840 --> 00:18:54,760
And that's why, no matter what,
I won't let you in the barrier.

331
00:18:55,680 --> 00:18:56,640
Let me in.

332
00:18:56,780 --> 00:18:58,898
I look forward to serving you again.

333
00:19:00,460 --> 00:19:01,460
I give up.

334
00:19:02,240 --> 00:19:04,080
I won't be selfish anymore.

335
00:19:04,780 --> 00:19:07,486
But you'd better come
back to me in one piece.

336
00:19:07,700 --> 00:19:08,540
Hello there.

337
00:19:10,500 --> 00:19:12,860
If you die, I'll kill you.

338
00:19:13,180 --> 00:19:14,660
I'll help you.

339
00:19:14,980 --> 00:19:18,540
Even if you get buried, I promise
I'll come and dig you out.

340
00:19:18,780 --> 00:19:20,898
All you've got to do is wait for me.

341
00:19:21,640 --> 00:19:24,522
You're sacrificing yourself
to save your friends?

342
00:19:24,740 --> 00:19:27,740
Your determination amuses me. Thank you.

343
00:19:28,040 --> 00:19:30,497
I encourage you to consider something.

344
00:19:30,580 --> 00:19:37,000
I have been lurking within the confines
of a bracer upon Solreem's arm.

345
00:19:37,280 --> 00:19:41,297
It is an extension of me and
still very much attached to her.

346
00:19:41,380 --> 00:19:42,437
What's he all about?

347
00:19:42,520 --> 00:19:45,720
I'll show you why this
matters. What's happening?

348
00:19:45,880 --> 00:19:47,292
Voxo and the Netherlord.

349
00:19:47,560 --> 00:19:48,500
What the heck?

350
00:19:48,740 --> 00:19:49,681
Didn't we leave?

351
00:19:49,840 --> 00:19:53,428
That jerk forced Sulream to use
her blessing of transference.

352
00:19:54,160 --> 00:19:55,920
Damn you, bony bullet!

353
00:19:57,040 --> 00:19:58,540
Now then, Periol,

354
00:19:58,860 --> 00:20:02,801
I suggest you use your blessing of
I-Breach to remove that barrier.

355
00:20:03,060 --> 00:20:07,648
Unless you want to watch your son and
future Torber-in-laws heads burst, Ober.

356
00:20:08,400 --> 00:20:10,400
Dad, don't give in.

357
00:20:10,740 --> 00:20:12,660
What a brave son you have.

358
00:20:12,840 --> 00:20:14,300
Now make your choice.

359
00:20:14,520 --> 00:20:17,000
Refuse my command and you both die.

360
00:20:17,240 --> 00:20:19,769
Or erase the barrier
and I'll let you live.

361
00:20:19,980 --> 00:20:21,392
There's no time to lose.

362
00:20:21,680 --> 00:20:25,020
That's why I removed the barrier myself.

363
00:20:26,140 --> 00:20:27,860
Hm, well done.

364
00:20:28,200 --> 00:20:32,680
Let us delight in watching as this
permusing magic item is destroyed.

365
00:20:33,220 --> 00:20:34,396
Don't sweat it, Cap.

366
00:20:34,660 --> 00:20:36,542
I made the call and that's that.

367
00:20:52,200 --> 00:20:53,540
I'm so sorry.

368
00:20:57,800 --> 00:20:59,080
I'm so...

369
00:21:00,020 --> 00:21:01,180
979 damage.

370
00:21:01,420 --> 00:21:03,920
Durability has been decreased by 979.

371
00:21:04,640 --> 00:21:07,157
You are no longer able to
sustain your current form.

372
00:21:07,240 --> 00:21:09,005
Reverate it to original model.

373
00:21:46,720 --> 00:21:47,550
1,

374
00:21:47,633 --> 00:21:48,463
2,

375
00:21:48,546 --> 00:21:50,657
3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 7, 8, 8, 9, 10, 10, 11, 11,

376
00:21:50,740 --> 00:21:55,900
12, 13, 13, 14, 14, 15,
15, 16, 16, 17, 16, 17, 17.

377
00:22:01,540 --> 00:22:02,940
Lamas

378
00:22:36,080 --> 00:22:38,360
I don't know.
